            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policies</strong><br>\nStalin's domestic policies emphasized strict state control, the collectivization of agriculture, and the development of heavy industry, combined with pervasive propaganda and an omnipresent security apparatus.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Succession</strong><br>\nStalin died on March 5, 1953, leaving a power vacuum and a legacy of fear. His death marked the end of an era and the beginning of \"de-Stalinization\" under his successor, Nikita Khrushchev.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nStalin's reign is remembered for its brutal efficiency in transforming Soviet society, its central role in defeating Nazism, and the fear and repression that characterized his rule.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
